-- The cast (n1): a projectile spell is an append — keys mint, parent records the caster, the muzzle is source-column math. Twin of n1-cast.bqn.
-- Noita, card by card: this folder rebuilds a wand game's spell system from ano's own primitives, no engine underneath. The first card is the cast, and a projectile is nothing but a fresh row.
-- Double Spell is the one-barrier batch: two prototypes minted in one statement, keys minted once across the batch, the drain beside them (§10). The batch is legal because neither spawn reads what the other writes; the .bqn witnesses the same law as mint arithmetic — one mint of two equals two mints of one.
-- Formation — Trifurcated: the replicate binds index per copy, the fan is polar math off the caster's own pos; each cast drains the wand in the same barrier it fires.
--! registry ../registries/n1-cast.reg
--! expect-n 7
--! expect keys = 0 1 2 3 4 5 6
--! expect parent = -1 0 0 0 0 0 0
--! expect sparkBolt = 0 1 1 0 1 1 1
--! expect bomb = 0 0 0 1 0 0 0
--! expect mana = 50 0 0 0 0 0 0
--! expect pos = 5 5 17 5 17 5 9 5 5 -7 17 5 5 17

Wand , spawn SparkBolt at pos + (12, 0) ; Mana -= 5
Wand , spawn SparkBolt at pos + (12, 0) ; spawn Bomb at pos + (4, 0) ; Mana -= 30
Wand , spawn SparkBolt * 3 at pos + polar(12, (index - 1) * 90) ; Mana -= 15
